301 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 193 0 R
/E (Another incredibly important way to recognize chord progressions is to understand that every different chord of a chord family has a specific emotional affect \(an "ethos"\); a dramatic character. Many musicians use these emotions as a way to identify chords. This also helps us understand why certain progressions are so effective. It's not necessarily about the intervals, it's about the emotional narrative they create. In music theory, this is an area connected to Functional Harmony.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
